  "question": {
    "text": "If the de-broglie wavelength of a particle of mass $(m)$ is 100 times its velocity. Then, its value in terms of its mass $(m)$ and plank constant $(h)$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "QleKT",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{10} \\sqrt{\\frac{m}{h}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "u7STz",
      "text": "$10 \\sqrt{\\frac{h}{m}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "n5FlA",
      "text": "$\\frac{1}{10} \\sqrt{\\frac{h}{m}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TQgcg",
      "text": "$10 \\sqrt{\\frac{m}{h}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the wavelength of given particle $=x$\nVelocity $(v)=\\frac{x}{100}$\nUsing wavelength formula\n$\\begin{aligned}\n \\lambda = \\frac{h}{m v} \\\\\n\\therefore &  x  =\\frac{h}{m\\left(\\frac{x}{100}\\right)} \\\\\nx & =\\frac{100 h}{m x} \\\\\nx^2 & =100 \\frac{h}{m} \\\\\n\\Rightarrow \\quad x & =10 \\sqrt{\\frac{h}{m}}\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
